# Keep the PRD in sync

`AI App Builder — Product Requirements Document.md` is the source of truth
for this project. Update it as part of the same piece of work whenever
something changes — don't wait to be asked.

## Section 24 — Implementation Status

Update this section whenever you:

- Ship or remove a route/page
- Change the stack, a dependency, or infra (hosting, DNS, domain, env vars)
- Deploy to production, or change what's live
- Add/remove an item from "Known gaps / not yet done" as it gets built

Keep it factual and current-state only — no history. If something moves
from "known gap" to "shipped," delete it from the gaps list rather than
leaving stale notes.

## Section 23 — Decisions Log

Append an entry whenever the stakeholder makes a product, scope, pricing,
brand, or architecture decision — especially anything that supersedes
earlier PRD sections (call out what it supersedes, don't silently rewrite
history).

## Workflow

1. Make the code/infra change.
2. Update the relevant PRD section(s) in the same commit.
3. Commit and push both together with a clear message.

If a change is trivial/cosmetic (copy tweaks, styling) and doesn't affect
scope, stack, or what's live, skip the PRD update — use judgment, don't
pad the document.
